# 🔑 Final Takeaway

The most important example is:

```java
final Student student = new Student();

student.name = "Nikitha";    // ✅

student = new Student();     // ❌
```

Why?

Because:

```text
student.name = "Nikitha"
        ↓
Changes the object


student = new Student()
        ↓
Changes the reference
```

And `final` prevents the **second** one.

### Remember:

> **`final` reference ≠ immutable object.**

A `final` reference tells Java:

> **"This variable must continue pointing to the same object."**

It does **not** necessarily say:

> **"The object itself can never change."**
